\begin{note}
We call a function \emph{recursive} when it calls itself.
A recursive function must have a \emph{base case} or it will loop forever.
In python, these "forever loops" triggere a \lstinline{RuntimeError},
but they are more generally called a \emph{stack overflow}.
\end{note}
